725" 13194139535094 true] [17592186330960 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535094 true] [17592186330960 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053562/assets/dd92f4b41c95c436027cce015b688df1a982f46913b0ea262f2d30e1e49259d5.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of the cubic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $-2.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}${x}^{3}\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$x\\,+$\n{{field-3}}" 13194139535094 true] [17592186330960 1113 #uuid "d1df841d-233d-5571-b2fe-b548c0a2b431" 13194139535094 true] [17592186330960 1145 "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2,3}=-1\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=-2.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2(x-2)(x-(-1+3\\text{i}))(x-(-1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -2(x-2)({x}^{2}-x(-1-3\\text{i})-x(-1+3\\text{i})+(-1+3\\text{i})(-1-3\\text{i})) & = \\\\ -2(x-2)({x}^{2}+2x+10) & = \\\\ -2({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+10x-2{x}^{2}-4x-20) & = \\\\ -2({x}^{3}+6x-20) & = \\\\ -2{x}^{3}-12x+40 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=-2{x}^{3}-12x+40.$" 13194139535094 true] [17592186330961 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330962 13194139535094 true] [17592186330961 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535094 true] [17592186330961 1041 "field-1" 13194139535094 true] [17592186330961 1104 #edb/ref 17592186330962 13194139535094 true] [17592186330961 1110 #uuid "71eec172-b52c-5418-b4c8-f8193b53a4fa" 13194139535094 true] [17592186330962 1034 "-2" 13194139535094 true] [17592186330962 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535094 true] [17592186330962 1111 #uuid "5d3d8e8c-7015-514a-83d5-689d89928164" 13194139535094 true] [17592186330963 1000 #edb/ref 17592186330964 1319